{
    "type": "game",
    "name": "Back to Hearth",
    "steam_appid": 2642760,
    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Calamity devastated all the houses of this small forest village, depriving it of laughter, conversation, and life. The main character now needs to confront the consequences of the tragedy, repair all the damage, and restore every home to order. They aim to create a sense of comfort in each house to entice the residents to return home.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2642760/extras/ed7b64b0cdcaa139b2d850d0aedb48d8.avif?t=1755159919\" width=600 height=336 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each house requires a special approach: in some places, you need to fix a well; in others, you need to repair a sagging fence; and in others, you need to clear the flower garden of weeds. There are no unimportant things when it comes to the warmth of your home.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2642760/extras/97c3c6363dc1d3afdb332f5818e89c4c.poster.avif?t=1755159919\" width=600 height=338 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2642760/extras/97c3c6363dc1d3afdb332f5818e89c4c.webm?t=1755159919\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2642760/extras/97c3c6363dc1d3afdb332f5818e89c4c.mp4?t=1755159919\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Fire is a symbol of home comfort, warmth, and life. After the house is repaired and put in order, you need to kindle a fire. After that, you just have to wait a little while.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2642760/extras/60f0a1c450d3355bfd84f64c66198c78.avif?t=1755159919\" width=600 height=336 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Back to Hearth is an exploration meditation game that focuses not only on houses and locations but also on the stories of the people who lived there. The houses are imbued with memories, personal belongings, amulets, and other narrative elements that reveal the stories. Each of them will become your own.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2642760/extras/3f8e41556cf875712aa2a29d747ea051.avif?t=1755159919\" width=600 height=322 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Revitalize abandoned homes with your warmth so that everyone can be where they belong again.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Calamity devastated all the houses of this small forest village, depriving it of laughter, conversation, and life. The main character now needs to confront the consequences of the tragedy, repair all the damage, and restore every home to order. They aim to create a sense of comfort in each house to entice the residents to return home.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2642760/extras/ed7b64b0cdcaa139b2d850d0aedb48d8.avif?t=1755159919\" width=600 height=336 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each house requires a special approach: in some places, you need to fix a well; in others, you need to repair a sagging fence; and in others, you need to clear the flower garden of weeds. There are no unimportant things when it comes to the warmth of your home.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2642760/extras/97c3c6363dc1d3afdb332f5818e89c4c.poster.avif?t=1755159919\" width=600 height=338 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2642760/extras/97c3c6363dc1d3afdb332f5818e89c4c.webm?t=1755159919\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2642760/extras/97c3c6363dc1d3afdb332f5818e89c4c.mp4?t=1755159919\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Fire is a symbol of home comfort, warmth, and life. After the house is repaired and put in order, you need to kindle a fire. After that, you just have to wait a little while.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2642760/extras/60f0a1c450d3355bfd84f64c66198c78.avif?t=1755159919\" width=600 height=336 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Back to Hearth is an exploration meditation game that focuses not only on houses and locations but also on the stories of the people who lived there. The houses are imbued with memories, personal belongings, amulets, and other narrative elements that reveal the stories. Each of them will become your own.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2642760/extras/3f8e41556cf875712aa2a29d747ea051.avif?t=1755159919\" width=600 height=322 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Revitalize abandoned homes with your warmth so that everyone can be where they belong again.</p>",
    "short_description": "Step into a quiet, abandoned Ukrainian village, left empty after the Calamity. In this short, meditative, and melancholic journey, you\u2019ll rekindle the hearths of deserted homes, restoring warmth and hope to the families who once lived here.",
